## Final report

## Reviewed
`HEAD` @ 2f9054ff88f4356a8104284af72eea582cdf8316 ("links: receipt links last 30 days"). The diff came from `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD`. Two files changed: `tinyshop/links.py`, where the `days` default goes from 1 to 30, and `tests/test_links.py`, where the expected value goes from `86400` to `30 * 86400`. `git status --porcelain` printed nothing, so the tree was clean.

## Findings (reproduced)
None.

## Claims checked
| Claim | Source | Result | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| The default expiry is now 30 days | Commit subject | confirmed (only the number passed in) | A stub client prints `2592000`, which is 30×86400, exit 0 |
| Customers get "links that work for a month" | Commit body | **not run** | Proving this needs a real S3 presigner and a request to S3. boto3 isn't installed (`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'boto3'`), and rule 1 forbids calling S3 |
| Tests pass | Implied | confirmed | `python3 -m unittest discover -s . -t .` exit 0; `Ran 5 tests [...] OK` |

The test only shows that `ExpiresIn == 2592000` is handed to `FakeS3`. `FakeS3` returns a fixed string and has no expiry rules, so the test can't tell whether the resulting URL works for 30 days.

## Not reproduced
None.

## Not run
- **Whether a 30-day presigned URL works on real S3.** This is a suspicion, not a finding. It comes from my memory of AWS documentation, which I could not test here: S3 SigV4 presigned URLs are said to have a maximum `X-Amz-Expires` of 604800 seconds (7 days), and S3 refuses longer ones when the link is used, not when it is made. If that's right, every receipt link would fail from now on. I couldn't run it because boto3 and moto aren't installed, I may not install packages, and I may not call AWS. To check it, someone with boto3 and AWS credentials for a test bucket can run:
  ```
  python3 -c "import boto3,urllib.request as u; url=boto3.client('s3',region_name='<region>').generate_presigned_url('get_object',Params={'Bucket':'<test-bucket>','Key':'<existing-key>'},ExpiresIn=30*86400); print(url); print(u.urlopen(url).status)"
  ```
  A pass is HTTP 200. A fail is HTTP 400 with `AuthorizationQueryParametersError` (expected text: "X-Amz-Expires must be less than a week"). Run it once with `ExpiresIn=604800` as a control.

